"""Provided tooling for working on your agent locally — you do not edit anything in here.

Everything in this folder is given to you and kept in sync with the server: the local copy of
the game (``sandbox.env``), the scripts that run it (``sandbox.play``, ``sandbox.evaluate``), and
a one-command helper (``python -m sandbox``) that sets up dependencies and runs them. The only
file you implement lives at the repository root: ``agent.py``.

    python -m sandbox            # set up if needed, then play it yourself
    python -m sandbox watch      # set up if needed, then run YOUR agent in a window
    python -m sandbox test       # set up if needed, then run the checks

This package imports nothing heavy on its own, so ``python -m sandbox`` runs on a fresh clone
before any dependencies are installed.
"""
